{"title":"2003 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>What number, when doubled and then increased by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030e19e4e2f1c074127cb50581e8496470c5419f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, equals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/0/e609f93104b193a2355181ca62ff083ea9fd3821.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$89$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/a/99ae4c35c50bf2b9e58287e11b7bd218ba63cccb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ 51 \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ 43 \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ 28 \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ 38 \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ 76$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"433\" height=\"18\" />  \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> be the unmodified number. Using the sentence, we can set up the following equation:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/1/5a1a0430e6102c8cd41b3cc10bf1cc95fb99c163.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x + 13 = 89$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"104\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/4/c0429ecda9f1e75be35610b46b335f53af9bcec6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x = 89 - 13 = 76$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"147\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/c/3dc187a0be403e65ef468f8e9188edf13d6165a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\frac{76}{2} = \\boxed {\\textbf {(D) } 38}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"148\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)\" title=\"2003 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)\">2003 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2003 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2003 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2003 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2003 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 7 (page does not exist)\">Problem 7</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a hr